{"book":16,"chapter":14,"rubric":"FROM ASSEMBLER TO C / GOING DEEPER / CHAPTER 14","slides":[{"title":"Language editions","sub":"Chapter 14 · -std","short":"Editions","main":"Pick the standard with -std; gnu11 adds extensions.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Language editions","The -std flag","GNU extensions"],"captions":["C89 → C99 → C11 → C17 → C23: standards add features and stay compatible","Pick the edition with a flag: -std=c11, -std=c17, -std=c23 (c2x in older compilers)","-std=gnu11 also allows compiler extensions: typeof, statement expressions, __builtin_*"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"e0","x":50.0,"y":76.0,"w":58.0,"h":30.0,"text":"C89","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e1","x":115.0,"y":76.0,"w":58.0,"h":30.0,"text":"C99","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e2","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":58.0,"h":30.0,"text":"C11","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e3","x":245.0,"y":76.0,"w":58.0,"h":30.0,"text":"C17","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e4","x":310.0,"y":76.0,"w":58.0,"h":30.0,"text":"C23","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a0","x1":78.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":86.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"a1","x1":143.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":151.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"a2","x1":208.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":216.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"a3","x1":273.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":281.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["gcc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic main.c","gcc -std=c23 main.c   # gcc 14+"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":28.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["#define MAX(a, b) ({ typeof(a) _a = (a); … })","// only -std=gnu11, not -std=c11 -pedantic"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":28.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[19.9,30.5]}]},{"title":"C99 legacy","sub":"Declarations, bool, restrict","short":"C99","main":"Declare where needed; VLAs are optional.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Declare where needed","Types and macros","VLAs are optional"],"captions":["Declare variables where needed, even in the loop header; one-line comments","bool from <stdbool.h>, <stdint.h> types, long long, static inline, snprintf, variadic macros","restrict promises no aliasing; C11 made VLAs optional: the stack can overflow"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {   // C99","    int sq = i * i;            // here, not at the top","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["#include <stdbool.h>","#include <stdint.h>","bool ok = true;  uint32_t id = 7;"],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["void copy(int *restrict d, const int *restrict s, size_t n);","int a[n];   // VLA — prefer malloc"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":28.0,"w":335.0}]],"cues":[11.2,24.9]}]},{"title":"Compound literals","sub":"Designated initializers","short":"Literals","main":"Temporary structs in an expression live to the end of the block.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Designated initializers","Compound literal","Lifetime"],"captions":["{.x = 1, .y = 2} names the fields, the rest are zeroed; for arrays — [3] = 5","(struct pt){.x = 1, .y = 2} builds a temporary struct right in the expression — handy for default parameters","A compound literal lives to the end of the block: never return a pointer to it; {} is the empty initializer (C23)"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["struct pt p = {.y = 2, .x = 1};","int t[8] = {[3] = 5, [6] = 7};","// the rest are zeros"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["draw(&(struct opt){.w = 80, .color = RED});","int *a = (int[]){1, 2, 3};"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":28.0,"w":335.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int *f(void) {","    return (int[]){1, 2};   // ✕ dies with the block","}"],"bad":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[17.1,30.1]}]},{"title":"Flexible array member","sub":"Struct with a tail","short":"Tail","main":"One block: header plus data.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Struct with a tail","Allocation","What not to do"],"captions":["The last member is an array with no length: data[]; the data sits right after the fields, in one block","malloc(sizeof(struct buf) + n): an honest size instead of the old data[1] trick","sizeof the struct excludes the tail; assignment copies only the header — copy the whole block with memcpy"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["struct buf {","    size_t n;","    char data[];   // flexible member","};"],"hl":[2],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"h","x":90.0,"y":76.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"n = 5","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c0","x":150.0,"y":76.0,"w":34.0,"h":30.0,"text":"h","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c1","x":186.0,"y":76.0,"w":34.0,"h":30.0,"text":"e","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c2","x":222.0,"y":76.0,"w":34.0,"h":30.0,"text":"l","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c3","x":258.0,"y":76.0,"w":34.0,"h":30.0,"text":"l","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c4","x":294.0,"y":76.0,"w":34.0,"h":30.0,"text":"o","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"malloc(sizeof *b + 5)","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["struct buf a = *b;   // ✕ no tail","memcpy(c, b, sizeof *b + b->n);   // ✓"],"hl":[1],"bad":[0],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":28.0,"w":335.0}]],"cues":[11.1,28.4]}]},{"title":"restrict and inline","sub":"Promises to the compiler","short":"restrict","main":"Never break restrict; static inline goes in headers.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["restrict","memcpy and memmove","static inline"],"captions":["restrict is a promise: nobody else changes this memory through another pointer; the compiler optimizes harder","memcpy takes restrict: overlapping regions are UB; memmove is for overlapping","Headers use static inline: each file gets its own copy, and the compiler decides whether to inline"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["void add(int *restrict a, const int *restrict b) {","    *a += *b;   // *b can stay in a register","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["void *memcpy(void *restrict d, const void *restrict s, size_t n);","void *memmove(void *d, const void *s, size_t n);"],"lang":"c","size":8.5,"lh":30.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["static inline int sq(int x) {","    return x * x;","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[7.4,25.5]}]},{"title":"C11 checks","sub":"_Static_assert, _Alignas","short":"C11","main":"Compile-time checks and anonymous members.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["_Static_assert","_Alignas and _Alignof","Anonymous members"],"captions":["_Static_assert(condition, \"text\") stops the build: struct size, type width, constants","_Alignas(n) sets an object's alignment, _Alignof(T) reads it; _Noreturn — the function never returns","Anonymous structs and unions: nested fields become fields of the outer struct"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["_Static_assert(sizeof(struct hdr) == 8,","                \"hdr: extra padding\");"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":28.0,"w":345.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["_Alignas(64) char cache_line[64];","size_t a = _Alignof(double);   // 8","_Noreturn void die(const char *m);"],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["struct v {","    union { float f; uint32_t bits; };   // anonymous","};","v.bits = 0;   // no v.u.bits"],"hl":[1,3],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":335.0}]],"cues":[13.4,27.9]}]},{"title":"Atomic operations","sub":"stdatomic.h","short":"Atomics","main":"fetch_add and CAS are indivisible; data races are UB.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Atomic type","fetch_add and CAS","Data race"],"captions":["atomic_int guarantees whole reads and writes; atomic_load, atomic_store","atomic_fetch_add and compare_exchange are indivisible read-modify-write; on RISC-V they are amoadd and an lr / sc pair","A plain variable read and written by two threads at once is a data race and undefined behavior"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["#include <stdatomic.h>","atomic_int counter = 0;","atomic_store(&counter, 5);"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["atomic_fetch_add(&counter, 1);","int e = 5;","atomic_compare_exchange_strong(&counter, &e, 9);"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":26.0,"w":345.0},{"t":"code","id":"a","x":220.0,"y":118.0,"lines":["amoadd.w a5, a4, (a0)"],"lang":"asm","size":7.5,"lh":14.0,"w":135.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int plain = 0;               // thread A: plain++","                             // thread B: plain++","// ✕ data race → UB"],"bad":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":26.0,"w":335.0}]],"cues":[17.9,28.1]}]},{"title":"Memory model","sub":"acquire / release","short":"Memory","main":"Memory orders and the CAS loop.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Orders","release / acquire","CAS loop"],"captions":["relaxed — atomicity only; acquire and release pair up as \"after the write — before the read\"; seq_cst — strictest, the default","Thread A prepares data and writes the flag with release; thread B reads the flag with acquire — and safely sees the data","Build your own atomic operations with a loop: read, compute the new value, try to swap, retry on failure"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"relaxed","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":76.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"acquire / release","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":90.0,"y":112.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"seq_cst","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":280.0,"y":76.0,"text":"weaker →\nstricter","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":10.0,"y":28.0,"lines":["// A:  data = 42;","       atomic_store_explicit(&ready, 1, memory_order_release);","// B:  while (!atomic_load_explicit(&ready, memory_order_acquire));","       use(data);   // sees 42"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"c","size":8.0,"lh":24.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["int old = atomic_load(&x);","while (!atomic_compare_exchange_weak(&x, &old, old * 2))","    ;   // old was updated — retry"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":24.0,"w":345.0}]],"cues":[19.5,30.6]}]},{"title":"Unicode","sub":"char16_t, char32_t, u8","short":"Unicode","main":"Bytes are not characters.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["char16_t, char32_t","u8 literals","Bytes ≠ characters"],"captions":["<uchar.h>: char16_t and char32_t; wchar_t is platform-dependent and unfit for data exchange","u8\"…\" guarantees UTF-8; C23 adds the char8_t type and u8'a' literals","A C string is an array of bytes: length in bytes is not the number of characters (see the data representation chapter)"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["#include <uchar.h>","char32_t c = U'€';   // 0x20AC","char16_t s[] = u\"é\";"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const char *a = u8\"héllo\";","char8_t c = u8'a';     // C23"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"\"é\" = 2 bytes","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":250.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"1 character","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.6,20.8]}]},{"title":"C23: the language","sub":"nullptr, constexpr, attributes","short":"C23","main":"Keywords, constants and standard attributes.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["nullptr, bool","constexpr, typeof, auto","Attributes and literals"],"captions":["nullptr is a distinct null-pointer type; bool, true and false became keywords","constexpr — named constants for expressions; typeof and restricted auto deduce the type from the initializer","[[nodiscard]], [[maybe_unused]], [[fallthrough]]; binary literals 0b1010, digit separator 1'000'000; #embed inserts a file as a byte array"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int *p = nullptr;","bool ok = true;   // no <stdbool.h>"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["constexpr int N = 8;","int buf[N];","typeof(N) k = N;","auto x = 3.5;   // double"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["[[nodiscard]] int parse(const char *);","int mask = 0b1010;   long big = 1'000'000;","switch (k) { case 1: f(); [[fallthrough]]; case 2: … }"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":8.5,"lh":24.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[14.4,29.9]}]},{"title":"C23: the library","sub":"stdckdint, stdbit","short":"Library","main":"Overflow-checked arithmetic and bit functions.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["stdckdint.h","stdbit.h","Other"],"captions":["ckd_add, ckd_sub, ckd_mul: overflow-checked arithmetic — returns a flag, writes the result through a pointer","<stdbit.h>: stdc_count_ones, stdc_leading_zeros, stdc_trailing_zeros, rotations — instead of homemade __builtin_*","enum with a base type, _BitInt(N), strdup/strndup in the standard, #elifdef, __VA_OPT__, empty initializer {}"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["#include <stdckdint.h>","int r;","if (ckd_add(&r, a, b)) /* overflow */;"],"hl":[2],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":335.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["#include <stdbit.h>","stdc_count_ones(0xFFu)       // 8","stdc_leading_zeros(1u)       // 31"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":335.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["enum color : unsigned char { RED, GREEN };","unsigned _BitInt(12) x = 4095;","struct s v = {};"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":335.0}]],"cues":[14.4,29.6]}]},{"title":"In practice","sub":"What to enable and what to avoid","short":"In practice","main":"C11+ and warnings; check C23 support.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["What to enable","What to avoid","Portability"],"captions":["Standard C11 or newer; -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic; stdint and bool; size_t for sizes; designated initializers, const, restrict, static_assert, attributes","VLAs, register, gets and unsafe strcpy/sprintf; compiler extensions where portability matters","For C23, check support for each feature: compilers adopt it gradually"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"-std=c11 -Wall -Wextra","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":86.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"stdint, bool, size_t","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":90.0,"y":122.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"static_assert, const","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"VLA, register","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":86.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"gets, strcpy, sprintf","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":90.0,"y":122.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"extensions everywhere","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["#if __STDC_VERSION__ >= 202311L","    /* C23 */","#endif"],